{"title":"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a ten-mile race <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d89fb502616ee0a92bf8184bc6884a4e0b39f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{First}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"11\" /> beats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcbeee0f2c6fcc57f1b78f153174c850497f1e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{Second}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d89fb502616ee0a92bf8184bc6884a4e0b39f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{First}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"11\" /> beats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e243a46378c220181ca7ad3904136f1f2299671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{Third}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles. \nIf the runners maintain constant speeds throughout the race, \nby how many miles does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcbeee0f2c6fcc57f1b78f153174c850497f1e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{Second}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> beat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e243a46378c220181ca7ad3904136f1f2299671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{Third}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c774fda7d68a38ff95f0bc723c6ab79aa9e99dd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{4}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\frac{3}{4}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"388\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the time First finishes the race, Second has run <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115e11f472361e53f627a66417f96cdfed51a037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> miles while Third has run <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58b33e339e3c1799386ad9722fe37268121da1f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-4=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> miles.  Thus Third's speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a1275c229b0561bbbe97d3d81237e85964a78efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{8} = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> of Second's speed.\n</p><p>Therefore, when Second finishes the race, Third has run <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e2364ae58012109e2425abe5814ad30acc0be74b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 10 = \\frac{15}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> miles.  So Second beats Third by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fb0c9cc5c5c2c28b7ea34020853506c738bf8f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - \\frac{15}{2} = \\frac{5}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"194\" height=\"49\" /> miles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME\" title=\"1964 AHSME\">1964 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1964 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1964\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/P